<h3 id="instagram-feed">Instagram Feed</h3>
<p>
	The Default, Jungle and Fab demos show an Instagram feed with the <strong>Smash Balloon Social Photo Feed</strong> plugin. The imported pages already contain its <code>[instagram-feed]</code> shortcode, so you only need to connect your Instagram account. Until you do, visitors see no feed there.
</p>
<ol>
	<li>Install and activate Smash Balloon Social Photo Feed from <strong>Appearance &gt; Install Plugins</strong>.</li>
	<li>Go to <strong>Instagram Feed &gt; All Feeds</strong>, click <strong>Add New</strong>, choose <strong>User Timeline</strong> and add your account as a source. Follow the plugin's prompts to connect it.</li>
	<li>Customize and save the feed.</li>
</ol>
<p>
	The <code>[instagram-feed]</code> shortcode shows the first feed you create. To show a different feed, click <strong>Embed</strong> on that feed, copy its shortcode and use it in place of <code>[instagram-feed]</code> on the page. For account requirements and connection help, follow <a href="https://smashballoon.com/doc/setting-up-the-free-instagram-feed-wordpress-plugin/" target="_blank">Smash Balloon's setup guide</a>.
</p>

